WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:11.160
10. Postmodern architecture. Postmodern architecture began as a reaction against

2
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:18.600
modernist architecture. Modernist architecture was very formal, functional, and often plain.

3
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:24.680
Postmodern architecture is seen as a return to cleverness and fun. Postmodern buildings

4
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:31.040
have parts that are only for decoration, rather than being strictly useful. Many postmodern

5
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:37.760
buildings take architectural styles from the past and use them in new, interesting, or funny ways.

6
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:45.440
For example, the Sony building in New York is a skyscraper with an elaborate top that looks like

7
00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:52.520
an old bookcase. There was no need for that kind of decoration, but it is beautiful and funny.

8
00:00:52.520 --> 00:01:00.880
Postmodern architecture values decoration and function. What we call postmodern architecture

9
00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:08.800
began in the United States in the 1960s. One early important figure was Robert Venturi. His

10
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:16.240
Vanna Venturi house is a classic postmodern building. Venturi built a gabled roof, that is,

11
00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:23.240
a roof that forms a peak in the center on that house. But the peak is split in the middle, so

12
00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:28.680
the functional gabled roof, which was designed to allow rain and snow to run down the side,

13
00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:37.160
is turned into art instead. Charles Moore is another famous postmodern architect. One well-known

14
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:45.080
work of his is the Piazza d'Italia in New Orleans. His Piazza d'Italia uses many old Italian-style

15
00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:51.800
posts, but they aren't made of traditional materials. Some of them, in fact, are made using

16
00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:59.240
jets of water. In the late 1980s, a type of architecture called deconstructivism developed

17
00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:05.720
out of the postmodern movement. This style takes apart buildings and tries to separate elements

18
00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:13.640
usually found together. It is a very unusual, striking style. Postmodernism in all its forms

19
00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:19.720
is alive and inspiring. It is still a main influence on architects around the world.
